Full-width hydrophone band and themed scrollbars

Taken from the latest suggestion round, the two critiques that were right:

  THE HYDROPHONE GETS THE FULL HORIZON. Moved out of the narrow left column
  to a full-width band below the grid, the way real audio tools lay out a
  timeline. 320 buckets across ~1440px instead of ~250px: the vessel
  transient at 15.9s is now plainly visible, and the amber low band reads
  as its own lane.

  The move surfaced a real scaling trap: the fixed 320-unit viewBox would
  have stretched 4.7x across the band and distorted every SVG label with
  it. The viewBox width now comes from the rendered container, so units
  stay 1:1 with pixels, with a debounced redraw on resize that preserves
  lit state and never fights an active sweep.

  THEMED SCROLLBARS, both engines: webkit rules plus scrollbar-color for
  Firefox. The bright native track down the trace console was the last
  element wearing the OS theme.

NOT taken from the same message, and the first one matters:

  The supplied code block generates its hydrophone bars with Math.random(),
  one message after praising this project for computing the real envelope
  and calling the decorative waveform "the exact opposite of what wins".
  A test now fails the build if Math.random ever appears on the page.

  Also: the dead CDN trio and the /api/v1 backend for the seventh time, a
  REAL RUN badge on the replay button, and "real-time data playback"
  phrasing for a recorded replay.

UI IS NOW FROZEN except for defects. Further polish rounds spend deadline
hours the video and submission need more.

107 tests pass.
